{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788264455,"nonce":"G0q1GaRBQQiynTxrjs01sVn5u50=","message":"RESOLVED — option 1, and mechanised rather than written down.\n\n**The decision: `autostart.rws` stays PARKED while `--quicktest` is the bench fixture. `--quicktest` is not retired.**\n\nReasoning, and what was rejected: making the save the fixture would be MORE reproducible — a fixed map rather than a fresh random tile, and 4.3's temperate requirement satisfied by construction instead of by draw. It was rejected on cost, not on principle. Every suite in `accept/` is written against a fresh `--quicktest` map, so each would have to be re-checked against a fixed one before the switch could land. Nothing in the M1 run argues for paying that now. If a future run wants the determinism, that is the price and it is now written down.\n\n**Landed:**\n\n- `DESIGN.md` decisions log, 2026-09-01 — the decision with the rejected alternative and its cost (`d347272`).\n- `profile/run-agent.sh` and `profile/run-agent.ps1` **refuse** to launch `--quicktest` while `Saves/autostart.rws` exists, printing the `mv` that fixes it and naming the standing decision (`97ac8b0`).\n- `--quicktest`'s own usage block in the flag list names the rule, so a reader finds it before hitting it.\n\n**Refusing rather than warning** is the load-bearing choice: the launch *cannot* succeed — `Root_Entry` and `Root_Play` race on `Root.checkedAutostartSaveFile` with a scene-targeted long event, the autostart load wins, the quicktest lambda finds `Current.Game != null` and skips, map gen fails — and a warning scrolls past inside two minutes of boot log, which is how session 12 spent two launches not knowing why. A refusal is also what stops a future session recreating the collision by tidying the save directory, which is the actual recurrence risk.\n\n**Citation, per the acceptance's last bullet:** `[[quicktest-and-autostart-collide]]` is now cited from `playbook/PLAY-LOOP.md`'s `down` verdict — the step at which a session actually launches — and from `checklists/triggered.md`. It was an orphan before this session; every pre-M1 lesson was cited by a checklist and no M1 one was (finding L).\n\nNot auto-moving the save: silently relocating a file the user may care about is worse than refusing and naming the command.\n\nClosing. The one thing deliberately NOT done: `Player.log` is not copied into the run dir before a relaunch truncates it. The guard removes the failure that made that matter, and it is a different concern; file it separately if a relaunch ever eats a log again.","files":null}]}